Article 6 (Planning and Communications Division)
(1) The Head of the Planning and Communications Division shall be a public official of Grade III or IV.
(2) The Head of the Planning and Communications Division shall be responsible for the following matters:
1. Establishment and coordination of major work plans of the Commission;
2. Composition of the Commission and operation of its meetings;
3. Establishment and implementation of the master plan for the management of high-level radioactive waste and approval of implementation plans;
4. Matters concerning public deliberation under Article 18 of the Act and the composition and operation of a public deliberation committee;
5. Inspection of producers of high-level radioactive waste and waste management business operators, and orders requiring them to take measures;
6. Imposition and collection of administrative fines on producers of high-level radioactive waste, waste management business operators, etc.;
7. Management of organization and personnel quotas and coordination of duties between divisions;
8. Review, coordination, and overall management of statutes, regulations, and administrative rules under the Commission's jurisdiction;
9. Establishment, coordination, and implementation of plans for publicizing major policies;
10. Media relations, management of public announcements, and briefings;
11. External cooperation relating to the affairs of high-level radioactive waste management;
12. Other matters not assigned to another division of the Commission.
